NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/server.Engine.activeRunForConv kind=method
  digest=b3:7193b16a0b9ab32018676d4a1590e3622d16eb54f8596d0a9d737239e1e12227 file=neo/internal/server/engine.go range=1073:1098 lang=go exported=false byte_range=45892:46842
  sig=func (e *Engine) activeRunForConv(convID string) string
  doc=activeRunForConv reports the in-flight run id for one conversation, or "" if\nnothing is live. Unlike broker.has(id) (which stays true for 2 minutes after\nsettlement so late reconnects can replay), this consults the authoritative\nruns registry: a run is here iff registerRun has fired and unregisterRun has\nNOT — i.e. iff drive() is still executing. handleConversations uses it to\nstamp `live_run` on the GET /conversations/{id} response so a fresh tab /\npost-relogin client can subscribe(replay:true) without waiting for the poll.
EDGES
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/server.Engine
  ^defines=matrix/neo/internal/server/engine.go

