NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/server.mcpAlarmController kind=type
  digest=b3:f4f5fdb981dc2c6b3b8406b6387b91489f99f77a8f0aa7096f4dda3abcb1e008 file=neo/internal/server/automatrix_governor.go range=220:228 lang=go exported=false byte_range=9104:9633
  sig=type mcpAlarmController struct {\n	tools *tools.Manager\n}
  doc=mcpAlarmController issues the Chronos alarm lifecycle through Neo's MCP tool\nsurface — the Chronos alarm_set / alarm_cancel tools (the design's "create\nthe AUTOMATRIX alarm via the Chronos MCP tool"). Neo holds no signing key;\nthe MCP server authenticates to Chronos on the agent's behalf (DID-scoped,\nreq 8.1). This is the production boundary to the external Chronos system; it\nis intentionally thin — assemble args, dispatch, parse the returned id.
EDGES
